    "notes": {
        "053c376c-efe9-4857-a4c3-f4e6ce02066a": {
            "x": 64,
            "y": 288,
            "width": 672,
            "height": 224,
            "content": "## ⚠️ Timing\n\nThe query returns one row whose `id` is the current UNIX timestamp, so every poll returns a row with a new id and NewRow emits it. It also uses the `?` placeholder (last poll time).\n\nThe first poll after the flow starts is skipped and the start itself only records the baseline, so the trigger fires on the **second poll** after start. The AfterAll timeout (420 s) must stay longer than two tick intervals of the instance. No tables are needed."
        }
